{
  "paper": "Aprea & Sbaiz (2025), Decisions in Economics and Finance, https://doi.org/10.1007/s10203-025-00508-x",
  "comparison_level": "METHOD SUBSTITUTION on the Aprea & Sbaiz NASDAQ100 universe (n=54), exact period/schedule. Aprea minimize an aggregate Delta-CoVaR (LSTM-estimated) under ESG/turnover/min-profit constraints; this benchmark keeps the exact-K cardinality mean-variance objective solved by PSO/SA and swaps in MASTER/TFT/PatchTST mu. Not a replication: different objective and constraints, reconstructed public prices. Compared on the shared ex-post metrics (period Sharpe, CAGR).",
  "notes": [
    "Fallback: the Cesarone/Refinitiv sustainability ZIP could not be obtained (saved link was a Dropbox login page).",
    "Universe = 54 NASDAQ-100 members (as of 2020-12-31) with continuous full history back to 2006-10-06, matching Aprea/Cesarone's 54-asset full-history NASDAQ panel by construction (not the exact same ticker set).",
    "Alphabet kept as GOOGL only (GOOG class-C dropped to avoid a redundant near-collinear pair).",
    "WBA adjusted-close overlaid from CC0 Zenodo DOI 10.5281/zenodo.12566460 (Yahoo no longer serves it post-2025 delisting).",
    "Dates and monthly OOS schedule follow Aprea & Sbaiz: daily panel 2006-10-06..2020-12-31, fit through 2015-12-31, monthly OOS 2016-2020, T_f=59.",
    "Paper optimizes Delta-CoVaR with PSO; this benchmark retains the thesis cardinality-constrained mean-variance objective and compares MASTER/TFT/PatchTST via PSO and SA.",
    "Reconstructed public data, not the paper's exact file -- must not be labelled an exact-data replication.",
    "mu-normalization policy: all models calibrated to historical-return scale (calibrate=true); MASTER is rank-only so all three transformers are compared on equal cross-sectional footing.",
    "WINDOWS: moment_frequency is 'daily' (Aprea estimate their moments on MONTHLY returns, but they minimize a CoVaR with no Sigma matrix; our substituted mean-variance objective needs a sample Sigma). On monthly sampling the matched Sigma window (longest conditioning window 336 trading days ~ 16 monthly samples) is rank-deficient for the 54-asset covariance; on daily it is 336 samples (6x oversampled) so Sigma is full-rank while mu stays window-matched (MASTER 67d, TFT 271d, PatchTST 336d). The realized period Sharpe/CAGR follow decision_schedule=month_end + periods_per_year=12 and are unaffected by moment_frequency.",
    "REFIT: Aprea update the in-sample window at EVERY monthly rebalance. Retraining the transformers 59x x 3 seeds is intractable, so model_refit=annual (6 fits) approximates it; moment_refit=match_models keeps Sigma on the same annual cutoffs, and the matched historical mu still rolls every decision (conditioning window, not a refit). Renamed from the obsolete retrain_frequency/covariance_mode/moment_mu_lookback_periods keys.",
    "PORTFOLIO: exact cardinality_K=10 with w_max=0.20 matches Aprea's u_i=0.20 strategy, under which their optimizer holds ~10 assets (Tables 7-8). The u_i=0.06 strategy (~16 assets) is a separate config if needed. w_min=0.01 (Aprea use l_i=0) is required to define an active position under the cardinality constraint."
  ],
